Title: Start in SYS: when HOME is not set on AROS
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: Without HOME the documents folder was "/", which on AROS is not a usable starting drawer.
Change: Use SYS: on AROS when HOME is unset.
Scope: AROS
Upstream: local-only
Verification: Built for mainline AROS x86_64 (GCC 10.5, SDK nightly 20261110); LibreSprite starts on nightly 20261113 (pool v1-1, 2026-11-16)
Removal: When the file selector work picks a better default.
---
diff --git a/src/base/fs_unix.h b/src/base/fs_unix.h
index a313f08e7d7cde7945ebd76e77dc748e302942cb..ed3fd00ed1f1c10423680116ad58d704c32eceb5 100644
--- a/src/base/fs_unix.h
+++ b/src/base/fs_unix.h
@@ -194,9 +194,14 @@ std::string get_user_docs_folder()
   char* tmpdir = getenv("HOME");
   if (tmpdir)
     return tmpdir;
+#if defined(__AROS__)
+  // No HOME by default on AROS; the system volume always exists.
+  return "SYS:";
+#else
   else
     return "/";
 #endif
+#endif
 }
 
 std::string get_canonical_path(const std::string& path)
